  "boundedBehavior": {
    "tables": [
      "Absolute column and first-row cell requests remain minima when their total exceeds a definite table width. Declared columns take precedence; percentage requests use the remaining space.",
      "Used width propagates through margins, inline and nested sizing, clipping and continuation layout.",
      "Intrinsic and paint preparation share row order, effective legacy border insets and empty-row column eligibility."
    ],
    "styledWords": [
      "Ordinary and script runs without separators retain word adjacency. Prefixes relocate the joined word; an unbreakable word may overflow an empty line.",
      "Authored separators, preferred breaks, emergency wrapping, nowrap, cascade importance and valid-value filtering retain their policies.",
      "Ordinary flow, float exclusion and first-line preparation use the shared fitting boundary; combined float and first-line appearance remains outside the broadly qualified profile."
    ],
    "emptyEdges": "Empty decorated inline siblings contribute their advances when deciding whether a joined word must relocate.",
    "hyphenation": "Later and middle runs consider the current remainder, every joined suffix, inserted hyphen glyph width and applicable character/consecutive-line constraints. Root closure repairs the initial hyphenation guard in ordinary, float and first-line routes.",
    "srcset": "The observed uncaught 100ms regex timeout on numeric input 1 is removed by reusing the linear shared finite-number scanner. Leading plus and nonpositive values remain invalid; decimal and exponent forms retain the existing reachable grammar."
  },
